# Requests to try with VS Code's REST Client extension.
# Start the server first (npm start), then click Send Request above each request, from the top down.

### Sign up as Maya: 201 (send it a second time for 409)
POST http://localhost:3100/auth/sign-up
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Maya", "email": "maya@example.com", "password": "maya-example-password" }

### A password that's too short: 400
POST http://localhost:3100/auth/sign-up
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Leo", "email": "leo@example.com", "password": "study12" }

### Sign in as Maya: 200 with a token (the requests below use it, so send this one first)
# @name signIn
POST http://localhost:3100/auth/sign-in
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "maya@example.com", "password": "maya-example-password" }

### The wrong password: 401
POST http://localhost:3100/auth/sign-in
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "maya@example.com", "password": "Maya-example-password" }

### Who am I, with Maya's token from the sign-in above: 200
GET http://localhost:3100/me
Authorization: Bearer {{signIn.response.body.$.token}}

### Who am I, with no token: 401
GET http://localhost:3100/me
